---
import { sitePath } from '../data/paths';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import PageLayout from '../components/PageLayout.astro';
import NextStep from '../components/NextStep.astro';
import { founder } from '../data/profile';
---
<PageLayout title="About eFactory" heading="Build. Ride. Learn. Together." description="Discover eFactory’s approach to motorcycle support in Suzuka, founder Etsugo Yanagida’s automotive design background and active involvement in motogymkhana." intro="A place to understand your bike, explore an idea and take the next step—with knowledge and practical support alongside you." eyebrow="ENJOY WITH US">

  <section class="story-split content-section"><div><p class="eyebrow">WHY EFACTORY EXISTS</p><h2>From “I’d like to”<br />to “I did it.”</h2></div><div><p>Wanting to work on your own motorcycle is one thing. Having the space, tools and someone to ask can be another. eFactory was created to help riders move forward with the things they want to try.</p><p>You do not need to arrive knowing everything. The aim is to work through your project, understand your motorcycle and make the next step part of your motorcycle life.</p></div></section>
  <section class="content-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE PERSON BEHIND THE WORKSHOP</p><h2>Experience, shared in practical ways.</h2></div></div><div class="profile-grid"><figure class="profile-workshop founder-portrait"><Image src={founder.portrait} alt="Etsugo Yanagida, founder of eFactory, in the workshop" width={340} widths={[220,340,680]} sizes="(max-width: 600px) 220px, 300px" format="png" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>{founder.name} · Founder, eFactory</figcaption></figure><div class="profile-copy"><p class="eyebrow">FOUNDER / EFACTORY</p><h3>{founder.name}</h3><p lang="ja" class="name-reading">{founder.japaneseName}</p><p>Etsugo Yanagida began riding at 16 and learned motorcycle work through experience and the help of others. That experience shapes a workshop where questions and learning are part of the process.</p><p>His professional background includes automotive component development and design at DENSO, along with design management involving quality. His published profile lists nearly 200 patent applications as an inventor. At eFactory, that background supports practical conversations about parts, reliability and motorcycle setup.</p><div class="profile-facts"><div><strong>Automotive development</strong><span>Design, manufacturing and quality experience</span></div><div><strong>Active motogymkhana rider</strong><span>JAGE Class A, as listed in the official profile</span></div><div><strong>Community & competition</strong><span>Organising Chubu-region motogymkhana events</span></div></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="content-section"><h2>The rider’s perspective matters.</h2><div class="note-grid"><article><h3>Learn through the project</h3><p>Supported DIY keeps you involved in maintaining and improving your bike. Equipment and specialist work have their own agreed responsibilities.</p></article><article><h3>Connect building and riding</h3><p>Motogymkhana brings motorcycle preparation, rider feedback and setup together. Ask about the member support available for riding and bike-setting questions.</p></article></div></section>
  <section class="content-section"><h2>Based in Suzuka. Open to your next step.</h2><p>eFactory welcomes riders from across Japan to its Suzuka workshop. If you are travelling from further away, confirm the project, preparation, language arrangements and appointment before planning the journey.</p><a class="text-link section-link" href={sitePath('/services/')}>Find the support for your project <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span></a></section>
  <NextStep title="Tell us what you’d like to try." />
</PageLayout>
